I know exactly why that happened!
Because the step is technically both "Completed" (which we just forced) AND "Active", Material UI is getting confused by our CSS. It is prioritizing the **Active** color (which is set to primary.main / blue) over the **Completed** color (green).
So you are seeing the tick, but it is drawing it in blue instead of green!
To fix this, we just need to tell the CSS: *"If it's active BUT also completed, force it to stay green."*
Here are the two small lines to update:
### 1. Fix the Mini-Stepper (in the DataGrid)
Find your mini-stepper in the columns array, and update the StepIconProps block inside the <StepLabel> to look like this:
**FIND THIS:**
```javascript
                    StepIconProps={{ 
                      sx: { 
                        width: 20, 
                        height: 20, 
                        color: isCompleted ? 'success.main' : (isCurrent ? 'primary.main' : 'text.disabled'),
                        '&.Mui-completed': { color: 'success.main' }, 
                        '&.Mui-active': { color: 'primary.main' }
                      } 
                    }}

```
**REPLACE WITH THIS:**
```javascript
                    StepIconProps={{ 
                      sx: { 
                        width: 20, 
                        height: 20, 
                        color: isCompleted ? 'success.main' : 'text.disabled',
                        '&.Mui-completed': { color: 'success.main' }, 
                        // FIX: Force green even if it is the "active" step
                        '&.Mui-active': { color: isCompleted ? 'success.main' : 'primary.main' }
                      } 
                    }}

```
### 2. Fix the Big Stepper (inside the View Modal)
Scroll down to the big stepper at the bottom of the file and do the exact same thing for its StepIconProps:
**FIND THIS:**
```javascript
                          StepIconProps={{ 
                              sx: { 
                                width: 32, height: 32, 
                                color: isCompleted ? 'success.main' : (isCurrent ? 'primary.main' : 'text.disabled'),
                                '&.Mui-completed': { color: 'success.main' } 
                              } 
                            }}

```
**REPLACE WITH THIS:**
```javascript
                          StepIconProps={{ 
                              sx: { 
                                width: 32, height: 32, 
                                color: isCompleted ? 'success.main' : 'text.disabled',
                                '&.Mui-completed': { color: 'success.main' },
                                // FIX: Force green even if it is the "active" step
                                '&.Mui-active': { color: isCompleted ? 'success.main' : 'primary.main' }
                              } 
                            }}

```
This ensures that the moment a step is marked isCompleted, the success.main (green) styling overrides absolutely everything else, and you will get a perfect green checkmark!
